{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1553819-suggestion-for-baali-wars-campaign","id":1553819,"title":"Suggestion for Baali Wars campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-09-14T16:14:43-07:00","id":1553819,"title":"Suggestion for Baali Wars campaign","content":"Dear all,<br /> <br /> I'm toying with the idea of a VDA20 campaign that starts in the Middle East, is centred around figthing the Chorazin Baalis, and encourages players to play Molochim Baalis, Assamites, Setites, Salubris and possibly Lamiae/Baharis, though it's open to all clans. Molochim Baali characters would be pretending to be from other clans.<br /> <br /> The reason why I picked those clans is because they are prominent in fighting the Chorazin Baali. They have different Roads and values, but managed at least at some point to agree that Baalis were worse. <br /> <br /> The coterie would consist of young vampires who are just being released from their sires' tutelage. Their sires are particularly involved in keeping an eye on Baali activities, so they put the coterie together with a mission to deal with Baali activity around Chorazin.<br /> <br /> I have to decide a year for the campaign.<br /> <br /> Should it be before or after the second Great Baali War? When did that happen, given the differing accounts in the manuals?<br /> Should we play before or after the birth of Christianity?<br /> I think the coterie and their sires are probably particularly old due to their being so watchful against the Baali. I may let all chars start at 7th gen.<br /> <br /> Any other idea?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T07:30:45-07:00","id":1553855,"title":"","content":"I'll help you with the timeline:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;Second City&quot; (after the war against the Second Generation):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">During his wanderings, Haqim embraces his first childe, an astronomer condemned to be stoned to death. After a century of its creation and watching from afar, Haqim decides to enter the Second City. Malkav is the first to welcome him.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-AR, pg. 8-9]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Saulot embraces Samiel in the Second City.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Sa, pg. 15]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Demon-venerating vampire War. Haqim leaves the Second City and returns with the sorcerer caste. For a century, Assamites and Salubri purges every single devil-worshipper in the Second City.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-AR, pg. 10]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Lasombra] embraces the first mystic.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[PGtHC, pg. 180]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;Second City&quot; (half a millennium later):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The first tribe establishes the Well of Sacrifices in Assur. Saulot destroys it and embraces the Three Baali progenitors.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 15-16]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">A surrounding city dies. The new adversary are called the Baali. Mancheaka leads the attack but she and her brood perishes. Survivors retreat to a cave where they meet ur-Shulgi for the first time.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-AR, pg. 12-13]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">3100 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">1st attempt to awaken Namtaru. Nergal was the God of Mashkan-shapir. He believed that a Child slept beneath the city and sacrificed the entire city mortals to rise him. Only the betrayal of his D'habi ghoul family and the powers of the Lasombra priests of Ereshkigal that flooded the city with abyssal darkness, prevented Nergal from arising Namtaru. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Historical accuracy: There is no known previous record of Mashkan-shapir during the Uruk period (4000 BC to 3100 BC) other than it was known that the city was occupied. Historical records begin during the Akkad period (2334 BC - 2154 BC).</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 18-19]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">2050 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Historical accuracy: Ashur becomes the god of the city Assur (Qal'at Sherqat). The Assyrian Empire begin to expand to the west into the lands of Anatolia.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-C, pg. 12] [Cb-Ba, pg. 17]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">2000 BC (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Nergal appears in the city of Assur using the name &quot;Shaitan&quot;. Learns that Namtaru\u2019s resting place is beneath Chorazim. Shaitan builds a temple in the city, finds Namtaru's body and takes it to Crete.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 21]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">1590 BC (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Shaitan embraces Cybele.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 66]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Shaitan demands for tribute awakens Set. Menele, still a mortal hero in Athens, Balthazar from India, Gangrel from the steppes, the Dionysian and his bacchante followers, the Lasombra and Toreador from Africa, all came to face the Baali. He is betrayed by his childe Hay-Tau.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Shaitan's last attempt to &quot;Open the Way&quot; in the Knossos labyrinth. For nine nights and days the Clans unite to stop Shaitan. Set's childer creates a cataclysm to sink the entire island.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Historical accuracy: The Minoan eruption of Thera, one of the largest volcanic eruptions in history. Dated between 1642 BC and 1540 BC.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DAC, pg. 170-171] [Cb-Ba, pg. 24]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">850 BC (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Troile rules in Carthage.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[LotH, pg. 63]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Shalmath goes to Tyre and convinces Eshmunamash to travel to Carthage. They both establish residence in Carthage.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[LotH, pg. 62]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Tanith embraces Sahar in Tyre.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DA: RoS, pg. 91]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">800 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Tyre becomes the private domain of Tanith.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DA: E, pg. 183-184]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Tal'mahe'Ra create the Nagaraja.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[V20TBH, pg. 21]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">4th century BC (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Azif is worshipped within the cult of Baal. He embraces Fariq in Mesopotamia and turns him against his cult of Dagon. Fariq is captured by mortals, they tortured him and is buried alive.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[TbN, pg. 57]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">218 BC-202 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Cybele aids the Roman Ventrue to defeat Hannibal.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Historical accuracy: Hannibal campaign during the Second Punic War took place from May/June 218 BC until the Battle of Zama in 202 BC.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 66]</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">200 BC (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Cybele suffers from a blood lust decimating the temples of her followers.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 66]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Foundation of the Court of Miracles in Alexandria by an all-female cabal of Setites.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[CabN, pg. 145]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">195 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Tanitbaal-Sahar embraces Sahar-Hannibal in Tyre. Tanitbaal-Sahar runs to Carthage and then to Rome. Moloch was to destroy Sahar-Hannibal but Tanith interfered in favor of her grandchilde.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[V20TBH, pg. 225]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">147 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Tanitbaal-Sahar receives summons from his sire in Tyre. He departs from Ostia but never arrived. He disappears from the pages of history.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DA: RoS, pg. 92]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">146 BC:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Helena betrays Carthage and gives information on the city to Camila.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[CbN2nd, pg. 109]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Gaius Marcellus is embraced by an unknown Ventrue in Carthage.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[NObN, pg. 17]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Troile and Moloch meld into the ground, Carthage. Cybele seals them in the earth.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[Cb-Ba, pg. 23, pg. 67]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">636-646:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Samiel makes a stop in a village en route to Chorazim. There he embraces Qawiyya el-Ghaduba and leaves her a first-hand copy of the Code of Samiel.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DA: RoH, pg. 92]</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Assamite warriors war with the Baali. As the Baali retreated to Chorazim, they capture Izhim abd'Azrael. Enraged, the warrior caste assault Chorazim. They find Izhim being focus of a ritual that cursed them as follows: &quot;As you thirst for our blood, so you shall hunger for all blood for all time&quot;. Antara is one of the Assamite warriors, while in Cairo the Dream Court deceives Abla to suicide.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[LS3-WatD, pg. 53] [Cb-AR, pg. 23] [CabN, pg. 95] [LotC, pg. 15] [TCCA, pg. 111-119]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">700 (aprox):</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Samiel learns of the infernal presence of Kupala and goes to the Carpathian in search for Baali. He finds the Eldest and they both destroy each other.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">The Eldest is later reborn within the Dracon.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">[DAN: Tz] [Cb-TzR, pg. 14-15]</span></span></span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T09:28:48-07:00","id":1553856,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hope this helps. </div> </div> </div>It does. Thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-09-16T11:45:00-07:00","id":1553859,"title":"","content":"That is a great detailed timeline Saga.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}